<title>USA: Hong Kong to maintain freedoms after takeover - Qian.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong to maintain freedoms after takeover - Qian.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chinese Foreign Minister Qian Qichen said on Tuesday that Hong Kong would retain its &quot;freedoms, stability and prosperity&quot; after China resumes control of the British colony on July 1.</p>
<p>Qian was speaking to reporters through an interpreter after meeting U.S. National Security Adviser Sandy Berger at the White House.</p>
